2026-09-11 08:20:36 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"a56cec5e-047e-42df-8630-9598f7ffb96c","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-aws-s3-file-upload/a56cec5e-047e-42df-8630-9598f7ffb96c.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/aws-s3-file-upload","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/universal_extension.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/universal_extension.md","content":"# universal_extension Module Reference\n\n`universal_extension` is a Stonebranch proprietary module bundled with the Universal Agent (UAG). It is **not on PyPI** and cannot be `pip install`ed. Any import error referencing it during local validation is a false positive — do not treat it as a missing dependency.\n\n---\n\n## Valid Imports\n\n### Top-level (from `__init__.py`)\n\n```python\nfrom universal_extension import UniversalExtension\nfrom universal_extension import ExtensionResult\nfrom universal_extension import logger\nfrom universal_extension import RequestType\nfrom universal_extension import event    # submodule\nfrom universal_extension import ui       # submodule\nfrom universal_extension import otel     # submodule (optional, requires Python >=3.7)\nfrom universal_extension import utility  # submodule\n```\n\n### Decorators\n\n```python\nfrom universal_extension.deco.command import dynamic_command\nfrom universal_extension.deco.choice import dynamic_choice_command\n```\n\n---\n\n## What Is Available\n\n### Core symbols\n\n| Symbol | Kind | Notes |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| `UniversalExtension` | Base class | Subclassed by every extension |\n| `ExtensionResult` | Result class | Returned from `extension_start`, dynamic commands, and choice commands |\n| `logger` | Logger instance | Pre-configured; also accessible as `self.log` inside the class |\n| `RequestType` | Enum | Values: `EXTENSION_START`, `DYNAMIC_CHOICE`, `DYNAMIC_COMMAND` |\n| `dynamic_command(name)` | Decorator | Registers a dynamic command handler on the extension class |\n| `dynamic_choice_command(field_name)` | Decorator | Registers a dynamic choice handler on the extension class |\n\n---\n\n### ExtensionResult keyword arguments\n\n`ExtensionResult` accepts kwargs that vary by context. UAG maps them to the appropriate internal result type at runtime.\n\n| kwarg | Type | Used in |\n|-------|------|---------|\n| `rc` | `int` | All contexts — 0 = success, non-zero = error |\n| `message` | `str` | All contexts — informational or error message |\n| `output_fields` | `dict` | `extension_start` — key/value pairs sent to UAC output fields |\n| `unv_output` | `str` | `extension_start` — payload appearing on the Output tab |\n| `output` | `bool` | Dynamic command — whether command produced persistent output |\n| `output_data` | `str` | Dynamic command — data returned and optionally persisted |\n| `output_name` | `str` | Dynamic command — custom name for the output data |\n| `values` | `list[str]` | Dynamic choice command — values used to populate a dropdown field |\n\n---\n\n### UniversalExtension — overridable methods\n\n| Method | Signature |\n|--------|-----------|\n| `extension_start` | `(self, fields: dict) -> ExtensionResult` |\n| `extension_cancel` | `(self) -> None` |\n| `extension_new` | `(cls, fields: dict) -> ExtensionConfig` (classmethod) |\n\n---\n\n### UniversalExtension — available on `self`\n\n| Member | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `self.log` | Logger instance (same object as the top-level `logger`) |\n| `self.uip.task_variables` | Task variables dict |\n| `self.uip.instance_id` | Instance identifier |\n| `self.uip.request_type` | `RequestType` value indicating what triggered execution |\n| `self.update_extension_status(fields)` | Push output fields to UAC in real time |\n\n---\n\n## Submodule: `event`\n\nPublish Universal Events to the Controller.\n\n```python\nfrom universal_extension import event\n\nevent.publish(name, attributes, time_to_live=None)\n```\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n|-----------|------|-------------|\n| `name` | `str` | Name of the event defined in the Controller |\n| `attributes` | `dict` | Attribute key/value pairs — values must be `str`, `bool`, `int`, or `float` |\n| `time_to_live` | `int` (optional) | Max event lifetime in minutes; defaults to the event template default |\n\n---\n\n## Submodule: `ui`\n\nPush state updates to the Controller without waiting for `extension_start` to return.\n\n```python\nfrom universal_extension import ui\n\nui.update_output_fields(fields)     # fields: dict\nui.update_progress(percent_done)    # percent_done: int in [0..100]\n```\n\n| Function | Description |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `update_output_fields(fields)` | Send output field values to the Controller mid-execution |\n| `update_progress(percent_done)` | Report execution progress percentage to the Controller |\n\n---\n\n## Submodule: `utility`\n\nPublic utility classes available to extension developers.\n\n```python\nfrom universal_extension import utility\n\nt = utility.NoOp(1, 2, \"anything\")   # accepts any args, does nothing\nt.any_method(\"call\")                  # returns self, never raises\n\nwith utility.noop_context() as noop:  # stand-in context manager\n    noop.whatever()\n```\n\n| Symbol | Kind | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `NoOp` | Class | A no-op stub — accepts any args, any attribute access, any call; returns `self` |\n| `noop_context()` | Context manager | Yields a `NoOp` instance; useful as a conditional stand-in for a real context |\n\n> All other names in `utility` are prefixed with `_` and are internal — do not import them.\n\n---\n\n## Submodule: `otel`\n\nWraps OpenTelemetry and exposes it for extension use. Only available when `otel.is_compatible` is `True` (Python >= 3.7, not SunOS).\n\n```python\nfrom universal_extension import otel\n\nif otel.is_compatible:\n    tracer = otel.trace.get_tracer(__name__)\n    meter  = otel.metrics.get_meter(__name__)\n```\n\n| Symbol | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `otel.is_compatible` | `bool` — `True` if OpenTelemetry is available in this environment |\n| `otel.trace` | `opentelemetry.trace` module |\n| `otel.metrics` | `opentelemetry.metrics` module |\n| `otel.baggage` | `opentelemetry.baggage` module |\n| `otel.context` | `opentelemetry.context` module |\n| `otel.sdk_trace` | `opentelemetry.sdk.trace` module |\n| `otel.sdk_metrics` | `opentelemetry.sdk.metrics` module |\n| `otel.sdk_resources` | `opentelemetry.sdk.resources` module |\n| `otel.sdk_trace_export` | `opentelemetry.sdk.trace.export` module |\n| `otel.sdk_metrics_export` | `opentelemetry.sdk.metrics.export` module |\n| `otel.otlp_http_trace_exporter` | OTLP HTTP trace exporter module |\n| `otel.otlp_http_metric_exporter` | OTLP HTTP metric exporter module |\n\n**Restrictions enforced by UAG:**\n- `OTLPSpanExporter` and `OTLPMetricExporter` endpoint/certificate cannot be overridden by the extension — UAG sets them.\n- Metric instrument names must not start with `ua.` or `uc.` (reserved namespaces).\n- At most one `PeriodicExportingMetricReader` using `OTLPMetricExporter` is allowed.\n\n---\n\n## Internal-only modules (do not import)\n\nThe following modules are marked `EXCLUDE` or contain only underscore-prefixed internals. They are used by UAG internally and are not part of the extension developer API:\n\n| Module | Notes |\n|--------|-------|\n| `extension_start_result` / `ExtensionStartResult` | UAG internal — maps `ExtensionResult` for `extension_start` |\n| `extension_choice_result` / `ExtensionChoiceResult` | UAG internal — maps `ExtensionResult` for choice commands |\n| `extension_command_result` / `ExtensionCommandResult` | UAG internal — maps `ExtensionResult` for dynamic commands |\n| `field_formatter` / `FieldFormatter` | UAG internal — deserializes field values from the Controller |\n| `ua_utility` | UAG internal — extension archive and dependency package deployment |\n| `exceptions` (`ProtocolError`, `QueueClosed`, `ChannelError`, `EAGAIN`) | UAG internal protocol exceptions |\n| `logger.ExtensionLogger` | UAG internal — do not instantiate; use the `logger` instance |\n| `outqueue`, `named_pipe`, `channel_manager`, etc. | UAG internal IPC infrastructure |\n","numLines":192,"startLine":1,"totalLines":192}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ehs11SWRmyKjGk1ci17GWW","duration_ms":4}

